# Research integrity

- Never invent citations, DOIs, values, sample sizes, methods or source locators.
- Mark each statement as source fact, computed result, inference or hypothesis when ambiguity is possible.
- Verify DOI and URL resolution before accepting a source.
- Keep contradictory evidence and explain the conflict; do not average it away without a method.
- A machine extraction is provisional until human verification.
- Report limitations and missing metadata directly.
- Do not claim novelty, Q1/Q2 status or state of the art without a dated search.
- Do not redistribute restricted full text or partner material.
